[block
  'ORD-0028-template-fills'
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-002'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'the map of the inclusion'
    '.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-INCLUSION.md'
  [/ctx]
  [tgt
    'what a template call carries never vanishes, by the inclusion the Regent decided on 2026-10-25: the commands inside a named fill, a named fill that names no parameter, and a template defined in the source and called in it; an ORD of the batch the version moves once for'
  [/tgt]
  [ctx
    'measured at b827782: collectFills keeps only the first literal of a named fill and the expansion replaces the call, so a command inside the fill is lost in the AST too; a named fill that names no declared parameter is absent whole; and a template defined in the source is not expanded by a call in the same source, only the store expands, with UndefinedTemplate suppressed'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'the Regent answered: slot on any element, so PACKAGE_TARGET section 4.4 widens and a carried command carries the slot of its fill; the source definition overrides the store, a second definition is TemplateDefinedTwice, and bindings inside an uncalled definition stop counting'
  [/ctx]
  [cnst
    'a command inside a named fill travels right after the bound value, carrying the slot; inside a placeholder the order is the bound value, the carried content, then what the hole held, so the way back reads it as one fill; a hole filled twice binds the first value'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'a named fill no hole takes lands after the body under its own name with TemplateUnknownParam at fix, the não sabe of the decision; a literal past every parameter lands after the body'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'definitions written in the source join the registry for the whole package, a call before the definition expands too, and a second definition of a name is TemplateDefinedTwice at fix; the AST keeps schema 2, the slot key optional'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'one declared source per new code, by M01, grows the snapshot with no existing hash moved; the Rust is ported byte for byte, held by new parse probes'
  [/cnst]
  [cmp
    'the fills'
    'the commands of a fill, an unknown fill and a source definition reach every projection and both ways back; each seen failing before it counts, and the Rust answers byte for byte'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
